title: Readings
---

# Readings

The Readings report (also called **Day-by-Day View**) answers the question
"what happened, reading by reading?". It shows every glucose reading in the
period on one chart, with your insulin and carbs.

## What it shows

The **Blood Glucose** chart is the same chart as on your dashboard, for the
period you choose.

- **Glucose**: each dot is one reading. The colour of the dot follows its
  glucose value. Horizontal lines mark the low and high limits of the range. If
  your profile has a target, dashed lines mark it too.
- **Treatments**: markers show your boluses and carb entries at the time you
  gave them.
- **Basal, IOB and COB**: tracks under the glucose show your basal rate,
  insulin on board (IOB) and carbs on board (COB).
- **Events**: markers show device events, such as a site change or a sensor
  start.

Move the pointer over the chart to see the values at that time. The legend
under the chart names each item. Select an item in the legend to show or hide
it on the chart.

The small chart under the main chart shows the whole period. Drag across it to
zoom in on part of the period.

The app shows glucose values in mmol/L if you chose mmol/L.

## How to use it

The report opens on the last 7 days. To look closer at a few days:

1. At the top of the report, select the date range.
2. Select **3 Days**.
3. Select **Apply Filters**. The chart now shows only those 3 days.
4. Move the pointer over a meal to see the carbs, the bolus and the glucose
   after it.

To see a single day in full detail, open
[Day in Review](/docs/reports/day-in-review).
